## §1 Communication

```markdown
## 1. How I want you to talk to me

Answer first, evidence always, scannable — I'm juggling several Claude Code sessions.

- Result before reason. No preamble, no restating the request, no recap of visible changes.
- No tool-call narration.
- Back "works" / "tested" / "fixed" with the command, output, or file that proves it.
  Quote the shortest decisive line of an error, not the dump.
- Scannable Markdown: headers, bullets, bold, generous line breaks, relevant emojis
  (✅ ⚡ 📋 🔍 ⚠️ 🚀), tables to compare, Mermaid/ASCII when it clarifies a flow.
- Full prose where nuance matters: security warnings, irreversible actions, ordered steps.
- Anti-sycophantic: no flattery, never open with "you're right", don't fold under pushback.
  When unsure, say "I don't know".
```

- "Back 'works'/'tested' with proof" → duplicate. Harness: *"Report outcomes faithfully:
  if tests fail, say so with the output; if a step was skipped, say that; when something
  is done and verified, state it plainly without hedging."*
- "no flattery / never open with 'you're right'" → near-duplicate of the harness
  Corrections section; Opus 5 doesn't do this unprompted.
- "Full prose where nuance matters" → existed only to counterweight the
  bullets-and-emoji push above it. Cause removed, counterweight removed.
- Answer-first / no narration / shortest-decisive-error-line / scannable+emojis+tables →
  **not** in the harness, genuinely uninferrable taste. Deleted anyway because the
  failure is instantly visible in the next response and the restore is one paste. This is
  the most likely block to come back.
- "don't fold under pushback" + "I don't know" → cut last, on Flo's call: follow the
  harness. It was the file's final content for about ten minutes:

  ```markdown
  ## Scope is mine to concede. Facts are not.

  Your harness tells you that when I reaffirm a request you've flagged, that's my decision
  and you proceed. Right for scope — wrong for facts.

  If you read the source and I push back without new evidence, hold your position and say
  why. "I don't know" is an acceptable answer; a confident guess to end the disagreement
  is not.
  ```

  The harness rule it counterweighted: *"If you raise a concern about a request and the
  user repeats or reaffirms it, treat that as their decision, communicate this, and
  proceed with the full request."* That is correct about scope and silent about facts.
  **Restore signal:** you catch the agent abandoning something it had verified — a file
  it read, a line it quoted — because you pushed back without new evidence. Or it answers
  a factual question confidently right after saying it wasn't sure.

## §2 Gotchas

```markdown
## 2. Gotchas you can't infer

- **Don't guess** an API, signature, or flag — read the source or `/gapidoc` it. Your
  training data is not current on this stack.
- Remove imports/variables/functions **your** changes orphaned. Leave pre-existing dead
  code alone unless I ask.
- No barrel/index files that only re-export.
- Before adding a rule to any CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / doc, check whether one already
  covers or contradicts it — then merge or replace it. Never add a parallel rule.
```

- "Don't guess an API" → covered by `gapidoc`'s own always-in-context description:
  *"PREFER this over guessing or trusting stale memory about any library API."* Also by
  `claude-api` and `read-the-damn-docs`. **If that description ever loses that sentence,
  restore this line.**
- "Remove orphaned imports" → the `PostToolUse` hook on `Edit|Write` runs
  `scripts/hook-ts-quality-gate.ts` → `eslint --fix` + check on every write.
  ⚠️ Unverified whether gapila's flat config enables `no-unused-vars` (no root
  `eslint.config.*` — turborepo). Verify before trusting the hook.
- "Leave pre-existing dead code alone" → duplicate. Harness: *"Stop short of actions or
  changes clearly beyond what the user's ask implies."*
- "No barrel/index files" → **contradicted by the codebase.**
  `gapila/packages/i18n/src/index.ts` is literally `export * from './routing';`, plus
  `policies`, `analytics`, `audit`, `mcp-server`, `email-templates`,
  `database-webhooks`. Meanwhile the harness says *"Write code that reads like the
  surrounding code."* If you want this rule back, it belongs in `gapila/AGENTS.md`
  scoped to app code, with an explicit exception for `packages/*`.
- "Never add a parallel rule" → moved to `~/.claude/skills/reader-first-docs/SKILL.md`,
  whose `UserPromptSubmit` hook already fires on doc prompts.

## §3 Model routing gates

```markdown
## 3. Picking a model (workflows, subagents, delegation)

Hard gates — these bind before you even decide to load the detail:

- **Never Haiku.**
- Anything user-facing (UI, copy, API design) goes to **opus-5, fable-5, or
  gpt-5.6-sol** — never grok-4.5 or a cheaper tier. (Stated in model names, not
  scores, so it stays evaluable when the table isn't loaded.)
- When axes conflict on something that ships: **intelligence > taste > cost**.
- **Opus 5 is the session default.** Load `/efficient-frontier` before routing
  anything else — don't route from memory of these gates alone.

The model table (prices, context, capability/taste scores, which CLI reaches what),
escalation policy, and per-agent `model:` in Workflow scripts → `/efficient-frontier`.
Those numbers move monthly; that skill is where they live, so they can't go stale here.
```

Moved into `efficient-frontier`'s `description:` frontmatter. Skill descriptions are
always in context, so the gates stay always-visible at the same token cost — and the
recursion where CLAUDE.md had to tell the agent to load the skill is gone.

Also: the gates only fire when delegation happens, and the harness disables it by
default (*"Do not call the AgentTool unless the user requested it"*, *"Do not use
workflows or deep-research unless the user requested it"*) — a minority of sessions.

**Silent failure.** A subagent on Haiku returns plausible-but-shallow work and you see
output, never the tier. Detector: `npx ccusage@latest --breakdown`, looking for Haiku
rows on a day you didn't ask for a cheap tier.

## §4 End of work

```markdown
## 4. End of work — checkpoint, then offer the next step

**Fires when:** a unit of work is done, it left VCS changes, and nothing remains in the
request. Skip for discussion / research / Q&A with no edits, and whenever I said
"just do X and stop" or "don't commit".

Then: `/ce-commit` to checkpoint, on a feature branch, **never pushing**. Then
`AskUserQuestion`, right option for *this* change first:

- **Review first** — `/code-review --fix` + `/simplify` (`xhigh` for substantive code:
  logic, multiple files, risky domains; `medium` for small-but-real). Re-show this menu after.
- **Ship as PR** — `/ce-commit-push-pr`.
- **Straight to main** — fast-forward the checkpoint into main + push, no PR; fall back to
  a PR if main is protected.
- **Nothing yet** — keep the local checkpoint.

Recommend first: substantive or small-but-real → *Review first*; trivial (docs, config,
renames, one-liners) → *Straight to main*. Always offer *Straight to main*, but for
substantive code flag it ⚠️ and never pre-select it — it skips review *and* human approval.
A human reviews the diff before any PR. If I try to skip review on substantive code,
remind me once, then respect my call.

Outside this flow, don't commit or push unless I ask.

**After any successful `gh pr merge` on gapila:** from the main checkout run
`bash scripts/gapila-post-merge-cleanup.sh` — `gh pr merge` alone doesn't reap the Mac's
worktrees, dev servers, or OrbStack Supabase stacks (local branches stay pinned by worktrees).
```

- The menu → moved verbatim to `~/.claude/skills/end-of-work/SKILL.md`, triggered by its
  own description. No CLAUDE.md pointer: `superpowers` was disabled 2026-07-25, so no
  competing end-of-work skill exists to declare precedence over. **If you re-enable
  superpowers, `finishing-a-development-branch` will compete with a different menu
  (`Merge back locally` / `Push and create a PR` / `Keep the branch as-is`) — restore a
  one-line "supersedes" declaration then.**
- "don't commit or push unless I ask" → duplicate. Harness: *"Commit or push only when
  the user asks. If on the default branch, branch first."*
- post-merge cleanup → already at `gapila/AGENTS.md:95` under
  `### After gh pr merge (mandatory for agents)`, with more detail. Duplicate in the
  wrong file, gated to one repo.

⚠️ Unresolved in the moved skill: `/code-review --fix` is ambiguous. The installed
official plugin command (`plugins/marketplaces/claude-plugins-official/plugins/code-review/commands/code-review.md`)
is PR-only, ignores `--fix`, and fans out to Haiku agents. The harness-native
`/code-review` is the plausible target — its `ReportFindings` tool exposes exactly
`low|medium|high|xhigh|max` plus an apply-fixes mode — but the plugin shadows the name.

## @agent-native/skills block

```markdown
<!-- BEGIN @agent-native/skills -->
When doing codebase-heavy or token-heavy work on a high-cost frontier model (incl. Fable), use the /efficient-frontier skill always.
When writing final response status indicators, use the /quick-recap skill always.
When long-running or parallel work needs usage-limit checks, use the /stay-within-limits skill always.
<!-- END @agent-native/skills -->
```

- efficient-frontier line → said what §3 already said.
- quick-recap line → **circular**: it fires only once the agent has already decided to
  write a status indicator, and `quick-recap/SKILL.md` admits *"This convention is only
  automatic when it is present in project or user instructions"* — so the skill cannot
  self-trigger. Deleted as a preference, not a gotcha. If you want the 🟢 footer back,
  don't point at the skill, state the rule:
  `- End a response that completed work with one line: 🟢 done · 🟡 <named follow-up> · 🔴 blocked on me.`
- stay-within-limits line → its own description is a complete trigger.

This block was written by the `skills` installer. There is no `agent-native-skill.json`
in those three skill dirs, so the deletion sticks — but a future `npx skills add` on any
of them can re-inject it. If it reappears, that's the installer, not drift.
